 request a hearing.\n4. **Order** granting or denying relief, issued if no hearing is requested or the request is resolved.\n\n**Rule 0-5 expedited review:** Requested in the filing, usually for applications substantially identical to relief the Commission already granted. The Commission decides whether to accept it, so it is not automatic.\n\n**The 45-day clock:** Rule 0-5 sets a 45-day period after filing for Commission action on the notice. It is a procedural marker, not a guaranteed approval date. Hearing requests, staff comments, and amendments can extend the timeline.\n\n**Caveat:** Confirm current rule text and staff practice before relying on this, since timing varies. There is no universal approval time.","ttft_ms":1846,"type":"result","duration_ms":2835,"uuid":"0b21bee9-f2c8-4906-be81-210a993eee55","ttft_stream_ms":453,"time_to_request_ms":74,"first_content_frame_ms":453,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
